udept — Installation
====================

Quick start:

    ./configure
    make
    sudo make install

Installs:

  - bin/dep                                       the program
  - share/man/man1/dep.1                          man page
  - share/bash-completion/completions/dep         bash completion (default on)
  - share/zsh/site-functions/_dep                 zsh completion  (default on)

Configure-time toggles:

  --disable-bash-completion    skip the bash completion script
  --disable-zsh-completion     skip the zsh completion function

Standard autoconf options (--prefix, --bindir, etc.) apply unchanged.

Tests:

  make check                 349 isolated Bats unit tests
  make check-properties      11 configuration-transform invariants
  make check-smoke           47 read-only tests against a real Portage tree
  make check-oracle          Bash atom matcher vs Python Portage
  make check-dist-inventory  source/archive test-inventory equality
  make distcheck             isolated archive build/install/uninstall check

The three Bats tiers require dev-util/bats, dev-util/bats-support, and
dev-util/bats-assert (the latter two are available from overlays such as
::guru and ::stuff). The smoke and metadata-backed property cases require
a populated Portage tree; unavailable per-test targets are skipped. The
oracle additionally requires Python 3 with the Portage module. Build the
program with `make` before running the smoke tier.

For the same static checks used by CI, also run:

    shellcheck --severity=warning src/dep
    bash -n completion/dep
    zsh -n completion/_dep

For detailed usage and architecture, see README.md and the man page
(`man dep` once installed). For per-release change history, see
ChangeLog.

Reporting issues: https://github.com/istitov/udept/issues
